This repository contains three kinds of code with different terms:

1. `vendor/zcode.cjs`, `vendor/cli-config.cjs` and `vendor/zcode-builtin.json`
   Proprietary software of Z.ai (https://z.ai). The runtime is the ZCode
   desktop app's CLI engine (version 0.16.5) in the patched form produced by
   kingsword09/zcode-cli's sync tooling (their MIT-licensed repo applies
   documented interop bridges to the extracted bundle), plus two defensive
   changes of ours: optional chaining on five property reads in the TUI
   turn-metadata formatter, and rewiring the `cli-config.cjs` require to a
   bundler-resolvable relative path. Every change is visible in git history.
   All rights remain with Z.ai. This packaging is an unofficial,
   non-affiliated interoperability effort; if you are Z.ai and object to this
   redistribution, open an issue and it will be taken down.

2. `packages/tui/` — the interactive TUI we ship
   Forked from kingsword09/zcode-cli (https://github.com/kingsword09/zcode-cli),
   MIT licensed, at their commit `b8d8e95`. `packages/tui/src/` is their
   `packages/zcode-tui` source (plus monorepo CLI helpers vendored into
   `packages/tui/src/cli/` with import paths rewritten); `packages/tui/PROVENANCE.md`
   records the seed. Our deviations carry `// [fork]` markers and are listed in
   `docs/tui/PARITY.md` §4. The legacy prebuilt artifact
   `vendor/zcode-tui-index.js` (+ `vendor/zcode-tui-LICENSE`) is kept only as a
   build fallback/reference until the parity gate retires it.
   Engine: `@earendil-works/pi-tui` (MIT, earendil-works/pi).

3. `test/helpers/terminal-screen.ts`
   Adapted from kingsword09/zcode-cli (MIT; see vendor/zcode-tui-LICENSE):
   screen-assert helper over `@xterm/headless`, extended here with cell-level
   color/style access.

